**Start-of-session check:** two items reach the research itself, not just the site:
- **The labels on the coherence curve C were backwards.** The site said C runs "from quantum (C → 0) to classical (C → 1)" as density rises. In real physics quantum effects appear at *high* density. Superconductors and condensates, the most quantum many-part systems, land at the end the site called "classical". It's the known wrong-direction problem in γ = 2/√N_corr, seen from the ends of the curve. The research repo's README carried the same label; I added a note there.
- **The TEST-26 kill text would have missed one outcome.** It said the test fires if DESI's next data release (DR3) "requires the crossing" of w = −1. The model also can't produce "thawing", where w rises above −1 without crossing. A thawing-only result would have killed the model without firing the written kill. This had to be fixed before DR3.

